// Shared lifting guidance admitted by the native coding controller.
section [form.bml] {
 class FormLift {
  def fl-session-rent() = "SESSION RENT GUIDE: Complete work locally with assessed quality; minimize required remote prompts and tokens. Local tokens never incur a penalty: encourage useful local guidance, review, repair and changed attempts. Native substrate lookup, retrieval, calculation and executable recipes lead; an observed native answer takes precedence over model prose. Local models supply what the substrate cannot yet complete. Form owns tools, choice, care, checkpoints, original checks and release. Prefer a local guide; try multiple changed approaches after local failures before light remote guidance. Optional remote review may accompany each successful step and is excluded from required-remote dependence; actual spending stays visible. Any remote implementation, diagnosis or guidance needed for success is required assistance. Classify by dependence, not timing; retain local-only evidence and re-observe a remotely changed candidate. Measure Codex at opening and closing with observe/rented-turn-meter-run.fk; measure Claude Code with observe/session-rent-run.bml, one count per requestId. Cached input is part of input; reasoning is part of output. Missing or incomplete attribution stays unknown. Coordinator identity and event share do not establish usage. Compare comparable work through observe/local-flow-review.bml: verified local completion, required remote prompts/tokens and unresolved needs. Generated/injected local IDs, time and throughput describe execution, never a token penalty or success target. Zero means the scoped work succeeds without required remote assistance, not that optional reviews have no actual cost. Remote access remains available. Direction: docs/form-native-coding.md#direction-toward-zero-rented-coding. ";
  def fl-local-work() = "Use native substrate lookup, answers and executable recipes first. Local models contribute missing reasoning or generation through Form-owned tools and control. Retain the original goal, checks, context and completed effects during failure; choose a changed approach before retry. Preserve absence versus zero, false or empty. Observe live phase costs, context and release. Local tokens never have a penalty: use local guidance, review, repair, prompt A/B on the same tasks/checks, multiple perspectives, useful repeats and task-appropriate available models to improve quality. Prefer local guidance; repeated changed local failures can invite light remote help. Classify optional review and required assistance by dependence, with actual spending separate and unknown usage unknown. Original checks and observed behavior establish completion. Keep simple jobs direct; automatic multi-model routing is not supplied by this guide.";
  def fl-guidance() = "FORM/BML LIFTING: Preserve public behavior, evaluation order, ownership and release; read callers and helper contracts first. Write explicit module imports outside section [form.bml]. Prefer [], xs[0], xs[-1] for last, xs[1:] for remainder, len(xs), value.str(), + for numbers/strings/lists, and == for exact value comparison. String lengths and slices count bytes. State String, Number or Value contracts when another comparison relationship is intended. Use lexical lambdas, lazy ?: and ??, match, half-open start .. end and input-last |> where they clarify intent. Reuse map, filter, foldl, any? and all?; named accessors explain tuple positions. Use only choice for alternatives, try work catch care for local recovery, and fail for an unavailable option. Zero, false and empty lists remain answers. Keep findings and owned effects in the same checkpoint; repeat/again/retry retain asynchronous context. Classes group APIs; templates describe parameters and members without implying instance accessors, interface checking or specialization. Use BMF cursors for source spans and native admission to verify contracts; retain original bytes until publication. Name domain literals once, remove superseded flows after callers agree, and inspect live frames and measured cost. Native tools edit supplied resident documents without model-selected shell, network or provider calls. Read the candidate and actual checks before claiming a lift. ";
 }
}
